 a lookup, defaulting to `-1` for values still on the stack at\nthe end.\n\n`O(n + m)` time, `O(n)` space, and the distinctness guarantee is what lets the map be keyed by value\nrather than index.","code":{"python":"def nextGreaterElement(nums1, nums2):\n    greater = {}\n    stack = []\n    for value in nums2:\n        while stack and stack[-1] < value:\n            greater[stack.pop()] = value\n        stack.append(value)\n    return [greater.get(value, -1) for value in nums1]\n"},"complexity":"O(n + m) time, O(n) space"}}
